Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:34:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [Xe2] Add BMG unit tests for the e4m3 -> half reorder
 atoms (default and CUTE_XE_E4M3_HALF_UNSCALED)

Runs Xe_Reorder<UU|VV, float_e4m3_t, half_t> on all 256 e4m3 codes and
checks every output bit pattern against a host reference:
- default path: out == half(e4m3), NaN codes 0x7F / 0xFF -> NaN
- CUTE_XE_E4M3_HALF_UNSCALED: out == half(e4m3 * 2^-8) exactly,
  NaN codes -> +-480 * 2^-8

The opt-in define changes the same inline atoms for the whole translation
unit, so its test is a separate executable
(cutlass_test_unit_cute_intel_xe_e4m3_half_unscaled); the default-path test
is part of cutlass_test_unit_cute_intel_xe. Both pass on an Arc Pro B70
(BMG-G31, DPCPP_SYCL_TARGET=intel_gpu_bmg_g31, oneAPI 2026.0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: riceharvest <myappleiddarimaan@gmail.com>

